          "kicker": "Injury blow",
          "heading": "Alex Mitchell has hamstring operation and could miss Six Nations",
          "body": "England scrum-half Alex Mitchell has had surgery in Finland to fix recurring hamstring problems, after four injuries this year. The 29-year-old was England head coach Steve Borthwick's first-choice nine last season. He could miss next year's Six Nations, as an estimated four-month rehabilitation would only give him a chance at England's final two matches, against Wales and Scotland. Any setback would leave him only pre-tournament friendlies before the Rugby World Cup. His latest injury had already ruled him out of this month's Nations Championship campaign."
