      "edition": "Friday 13 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Scrum-half reliance",
          "heading": "Steve Tandy admits Wales are heavily reliant on Tomos Williams",
          "body": "Wales scrum-half Tomos Williams played the full 80 minutes against Japan, the fifth time under head coach Steve Tandy that he has not been replaced. Williams has averaged around 74 minutes across those 12 Tests under Tandy, while Ospreys pair Kieran Hardy and Reuben Morgan-Williams have combined for just 48 minutes off the bench. Hardy has been ruled out for the season, and uncapped Dragons half-back Che Hope has joined three-cap Morgan-Williams in the squad."
        },
